# Vercel builds the Next.js application at the repository root and nothing
# else. Without this it also discovers backend/ and render.yaml, treats the
# blueprint's service definition as something to build, and runs the backend's
# install and migration commands inside a build container with no database -
# failing with a refused connection to 127.0.0.1:5432 that looks like a
# database problem and is actually a "what am I building" problem.
#
# The backend deploys separately to Render. Excluding it here also keeps the
# upload small: backend/ carries fixtures, a virtualenv and caches that the
# frontend build has no use for.

backend/
render.yaml
docker-compose.yml

# Local artefacts that should never reach a build.
*.db
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.cache/
